## Initial Q&A
### 1. On what specific date did Nigeria officially become independent from British colonial rule?
Answer: Nigeria officially became independent from British colonial rule on October 1, 1960, as stated: "Just after midnight on October 1, 1960, in Lagos, Nigeria’s flag was officially holstered for the very first time."

Source URL: https://metro.co.uk/2020/10/01/happy-nigeria-independence-day-2020-when-did-nigeria-become-independent-how-is-today-celebrated-13355032/

### 2. What was the officially recognized territory and borders of the Federation of Nigeria upon its independence in 1960?
Answer: Upon independence on October 1, 1960, the Federation of Nigeria comprised the territory of the former British Colony and Protectorate of Nigeria, which was divided into three large geographic regions: the Northern, Western, and Eastern regions. The northern part of the Trust Territory of the Cameroons did not join Nigeria until after a UN-supervised referendum in June 1961.

Source URL: https://www.britannica.com/place/Nigeria/Independent-Nigeria

